{"from":"1:4","body":"<p>That which the palmer-worm hath left. Heb. The residue of thepalmer-worm.<br/><ref to=\"JOL.2.25 AMO.4.9\">2:25; Am 4:9</ref>The learned Bochart, and others, are of the opinion that the four Hebrew words, {gazam, yelek, arbeh, chasil}, respectively rendered the palmer-worm, locust, canker-worm and caterpillar, denote four different species of locusts. See on<br/><ref to=\"EXO.10.4\">Ex 10:4</ref><br/>the locust eaten.<br/><ref to=\"EXO.10.12-EXO.10.15 DEU.28.38 DEU.28.42 1KI.8.37 2CH.6.28 2CH.7.13\">Ex 10:12-15; De 28:38,42; 1Ki 8:37; 2Ch 6:28; 7:13</ref><br/><ref to=\"PSA.78.46 PSA.105.34 AMO.7.1 REV.9.3-REV.9.7\">Ps 78:46; 105:34; Am 7:1; Re 9:3-7</ref><br/>the canker-worm eaten.<br/><ref to=\"NAM.3.15-NAM.3.17\">Na 3:15-17</ref><br/>the caterpillar.<br/><ref to=\"ISA.33.4 JER.51.14 JER.51.27\">Isa 33:4; Jer 51:14,27</ref></p>"}
