{"from":"2:13","body":"<p>rend.Here the word \"rend\" is used only once, but with two significations; in the former sentence it is used figuratively; in the latter literally--the heart not being rent in the same sense in which garments are rent.<br/><ref to=\"2KI.22.19 PSA.34.18 PSA.51.17 ISA.57.15 ISA.66.2 EZK.9.4 MAT.5.3 MAT.5.4\">2Ki 22:19; Ps 34:18; 51:17; Isa 57:15; 66:2; Eze 9:4; Mt 5:3,4</ref><br/>your garments.<br/><ref to=\"GEN.37.29 GEN.37.34 2SA.1.11 1KI.21.27 2KI.5.7 2KI.6.30 2KI.22.11 JOB.1.20\">Ge 37:29,34; 2Sa 1:11; 1Ki 21:27; 2Ki 5:7; 6:30; 22:11; Job 1:20</ref><br/><ref to=\"ISA.58.5 MAT.6.16-MAT.6.18 1TI.4.8\">Isa 58:5; Mt 6:16-18; 1Ti 4:8</ref><br/>for.<br/><ref to=\"EXO.34.6 EXO.34.7 NUM.14.18 PSA.86.5 PSA.86.15 PSA.145.7-PSA.145.9 JON.4.2 MIC.7.18 ROM.2.4\">Ex 34:6,7; Nu 14:18; Ps 86:5,15; 145:7-9; Jon 4:2; Mic 7:18; Ro 2:4</ref><br/><ref to=\"ROM.5.20 ROM.5.21 EPH.2.4\">Ro 5:20,21; Eph 2:4</ref><br/>slow.<br/><ref to=\"NEH.9.17 PSA.103.8 NAM.1.3 JAS.1.19 JAS.1.20\">Ne 9:17; Ps 103:8; Na 1:3; Jas 1:19,20</ref><br/>and repenteth.<br/><ref to=\"PSA.106.45 JER.18.7 JER.18.8 AMO.7.2-AMO.7.6 JON.4.2\">Ps 106:45; Jer 18:7,8; Am 7:2-6; Jon 4:2</ref></p>"}
